== the_plot_maps_no_y
error[Z0401]: `area` places each mark by its `x` and its `y`, but the plot maps no variable to `y`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:14
  |
2 | d.plot(x: t).area()
  |              ^^^^ needs both `x` and `y`
  |
  = help: map both where the plot starts, as in `plot(x: educ, y: wage)`

== a_band_without_x
error[Z0401]: `ribbon` places its band along `x`, but neither the plot nor this layer maps a variable to `x`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:14
  |
2 | d.plot(y: v).ribbon(low: lo, high: hi)
  |              ^^^^^^ needs `x`
  |
  = help: name it in the layer, as in `ribbon(x: educ, low: lower, high: upper)`, or where the plot starts, as in `plot(x: educ)`

== a_band_without_high
error[Z0406]: `ribbon` needs `high`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:14
  |
2 | d.plot(x: t).ribbon(low: lo)
  |              ^^^^^^ `high` is missing
  |
  = help: a band reaches from `low:` to `high:` at each row: name the two variables, as in `ribbon(low: lower, high: upper)`

