== a_frame_without_the_fill
error[Z0101]: no variable `g` in `the frame`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:40
  |
2 | d.plot(x: t, y: v, fill: g).area(data: frame(t = [1, 2], v = [1, 2]))
  |                             ---- this layer draws `g`, which the plot maps to `fill`
  |                                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not a variable of the frame
  |
  = help: did you mean `t`? If you meant a category level, write it in quotes: `"t"`

== area_of_a_frame
error[Z0401]: `area` cannot be called on a Frame
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | d.area()
  | ^ this is a Frame
  |
  = help: `area` takes a Plot first; `x.area(...)` is `area(x, ...)`

== an_edge_that_reduces
error[Z0401]: an expression mapped to an aesthetic cannot use `mean`, a function of `data`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:42
  |
2 | d.plot(x: t, y: v).ribbon(low: lo, high: mean(hi))
  |                                          ^^^^ not kept in a mapping
  |
  = help: a mapping is computed from variables, numbers, the operators, `case` and the functions of `core`, `time` and `text`, as in `log(wage)`, `wage / hours` or `year(hired)`; compute anything else with `add` first and map the new variable
